1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,801
RAM and storage are both memory.

2
00:00:03,081 --> 00:00:05,191
So why does your PC need both?

3
00:00:05,941 --> 00:00:08,261
Think of storage as a filing cabinet.

4
00:00:08,541 --> 00:00:12,164
It's huge, and it keeps everything, even with the power off.

5
00:00:12,444 --> 00:00:14,429
But walking over to it takes time.

6
00:00:15,179 --> 00:00:16,678
RAM is your desk.

7
00:00:16,958 --> 00:00:23,166
It's small, but everything on it is right in front of you, so the CPU can grab it in nanoseconds.

8
00:00:23,916 --> 00:00:28,256
When you open a game, its files move from the cabinet onto the desk.

9
00:00:28,536 --> 00:00:31,159
When you shut down, the desk is wiped clean.

10
00:00:31,439 --> 00:00:33,108
The cabinet keeps everything.

11
00:00:33,858 --> 00:00:37,618
That's why more RAM only helps if your desk is too small.

12
00:00:37,898 --> 00:00:41,869
For most gaming, 16 to 32 gigabytes is plenty.

13
00:00:42,149 --> 00:00:44,953
The full breakdown of every part is on the channel.

